# Use git mv for Moves

- Always use `git mv` instead of `mv` when relocating tracked files or directories so history remains intact.
- If a directory must be created first, run `mkdir -p` (or equivalent) before executing `git mv`.
- When multiple files move together, favor a single `git mv` per path to keep diffs tidy.
- Avoid raw `mv` in scripts or commands unless the target is outside the repository or untracked.
